 "section_summary": "This section contains pages iii-vii, Part One (pages x-xv), Part Two (pages xviii-xxvi), and the beginning of Part Three (pages 1-36) of a comprehensive statistical survey and institutional roster of educational institutions in Hokkaido Prefecture, Japan, compiled by the Civil Information and Education (CIE) Section of GHQ/SCAP in cooperation with the Japanese Ministry of Education. The introductory text and classification charts describe the national, prefectural, municipal, and private control structures of the Japanese school system, followed by detailed summary statistical tables showing the number of institutions, student enrollments by sex, and faculty counts as of April and November 1946 across higher, secondary, elementary, and special education levels. The remainder provides an extensive roster of individual educational institutions throughout Hokkaido—including university faculties, technical colleges, normal schools, secondary middle and vocational schools, municipal elementary schools, and local youth schools—recording each school's name, address, founding date, enrollment figures, and teaching staff.",
 "subfiles": [
